# Files exempt from swe's checks, on the `planning` branch only. A
# pattern with a "/" matches the path relative to this file's
# directory; a pattern with no "/" matches the basename, at any depth.
#
# This branch holds an append-only cross-session record, not shipped
# prose. The commit check installed by /swe:install-commit-hook works
# at whole-file granularity: a file needs a clean lint of its entire
# staged content before it can be committed. STATE.md accumulates one
# entry per session and already holds findings inside entries written
# by earlier sessions. Requiring a whole-file clean before appending a
# new entry would mean editing those earlier entries, which are a
# record of what happened and are not meant to be rewritten.
#
# The plugin's own shipped prose on `main` is unaffected: `main` has
# its own .swe-ignore, and each worktree reads the one at its own root.
# Note: a trailing slash does nothing here. swe's .swe-ignore reader
# handles no directory-only patterns, so a directory needs a glob.
STATE.md
tasks/*
